{"chunk_id": "49f1ad3850d4", "text": "As the tenth day of the Kurukshetra war approaches, the Pandavas execute a plan centered on Sikhandin, whom Bhishma has vowed not to fight because of Sikhandin\u2019s past birth as a woman. At dawn the Pandava army marches out with Sikhandin placed at the very front, protected by major heroes such as Arjuna and Bhima. Sanjaya describes both armies\u2019 elaborate formations and the devastating clash that follows. The Pandavas initially press hard, causing heavy losses among the Kauravas. Enraged by the suffering of his army, Bhishma launches a ferocious counterattack, cutting down soldiers, elephants, and chariots in vast numbers and terrifying the battlefield. When Sikhandin finally confronts him, Bhishma refuses to fight, reaffirming his vow\u2014setting the stage for the pivotal moment that will soon bring about the fall of the grandsire.\nPandavas place Sikhandin at the front against Bhishma; fierce battle erupts as Bhishma devastates their forces yet refuses to fight Sikhandin.\nThemes: battle formations, Bhishma's prowess, Sikhandin confrontation, war carnage, honor and vows", "vector": [-0.008702251128852367, -0.016997219994664192, -0.006788027472794056, 0.029297126457095146, 0.005131748504936695, 0.03988644853234291, -0.020907124504446983, -0.016861459240317345, -0.015721071511507034, -0.025183580815792084, 0.03250107541680336, 0.01959024742245674, 0.000990203465335071, 0.01653563417494297, 0.0062008630484342575, 0.013820423744618893, 0.03269113972783089, 0.0035874724853783846, 0.015476702712476254, -0.01887071691453457, -0.010596110485494137, -0.010799751617014408, 0.010243133641779423, 0.013257017359137535, -0.03486330807209015, 0.030057385563850403, 0.014933660626411438, -0.012639307416975498, 0.004032088443636894, -0.014512802474200726, -0.030328907072544098, -0.009625422768294811, -0.0033481945283710957, 0.0006715904455631971, -0.0375785194337368, 0.006323047447949648, -0.00980869960039854, -0.03714408725500107, 0.0